This is an upstream engine defect, so there is no in-repo `before` to rewrite. Two competing remedies, and the choice is a real trade-off:

Option 1 -- a narrow allowance (what 2 of 3 reviewers proposed as the default):
```diff
  const ALLOWED = [
    "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading 'voices')",
+   // NH-<new>. alphaTab 1.8.4's AudioWorklet output defers source.start(0) into an async
+   // promise while pause() calls source.stop(0) unconditionally, so a Pause inside that
+   // window stops a never-started node. Measured: 7/10 with no metronome, 0/20 with a
+   // ~700 ms gap. Remove this when the upstream fix lands.
+   "cannot call stop without calling start first",
  ];
```
Cost: CI goes green, but a real person pressing Play then Pause quickly still gets an uncaught throw, now deliberately ignored.

Option 2 -- withhold the pause until the output has started (adversarial's proposal):
```diff
- onClick={() => { if (playing) resumeAfterSeek.current = false; api?.playPause(); }}
+ onClick={() => {
+   if (playing) resumeAfterSeek.current = false;
+   if (playing && !outputStarted.current) { pausePending.current = true; return; }
+   api?.playPause();
+ }}
```
with `outputStarted` set false when `playing` turns true and true on the first `playerPositionChanged` with `endTime > 0`, issuing the queued pause from that handler.
Cost: a click can be delayed by tens of milliseconds, which touches how responsive the transport feels -- and the maintainer has already judged transport feel by hand.

Seed both halves of the pair the moment the engine sets only one. In web/app/play/NotationSurface.tsx, beside the existing useAlphaTabEvent subscriptions:
```diff
+ // alphaTab's own beatMouseDown sets _selectionStart and leaves _selectionEnd undefined, and its
+ // _onPostRenderFinished then reads _selectionEnd.beat with no guard -- so any render landing
+ // before the first drag move throws. Seeding a same-beat pair closes that window;
+ // _cursorSelectRange early-returns for a same-beat pair, so nothing is painted.
+ useAlphaTabEvent(api, 'beatMouseDown', (beat) => {
+   api?.highlightPlaybackRange(beat, beat);
+ });
```

